+# Fix SKU lookup, free-shipping threshold and VAT rounding
+
+Three reports from this week's order service use, each a deviation from the rules in `README.md`.
+
+## 1. Lower-case SKUs are refused (sales desk, Giulia)
+
+- Keying `lb-220` is refused as an unknown product; `LB-220` works.
+- Rule: "SKUs are case-insensitive and ignore surrounding spaces" (Products).
+- Cause: `Catalog.find` trims the SKU but does not upper-case it before lookup.
+- Acceptance: `lb-220`, ` LB-220 ` and `LB-220` all find the same product, shown as `LB-220`.
+
+## 2. Free shipping not applied at €50.00 (customer, Marco)
+
+- A basket of €50.00 after discount is charged €4.90 delivery.
+- Rule: "Shipping is free when the goods come to €50.00 or more, after every discount and before VAT"
+  (Shipping).
+- Cause: `shippingCost` tests `goods > FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS`, which is strict.
+- Acceptance: goods of exactly 5000 cents ship free; goods of 4999 cents pay the weight-band cost.
+
+## 3. VAT one cent low on some lines (accounting)
+
+- A single €1.99 item at the standard rate shows €0.43 VAT; the correct figure is €0.44.
+- Rule: "VAT is computed line by line ... and rounded half up to the cent on each line" (VAT);
+  "every percentage is applied ... and rounded half up to the cent" (Money and dates).
+- Cause: `lineVat` uses `Math.floor`, so 199 × 22 / 100 = 43.78 becomes 43.
+- Acceptance: each line's VAT is `percentOf(net, rate)` (half up); 199 cents at 22% gives 44.
+  Shipping VAT is already half up and stays as it is.
+
+## Traceability
+
+- Requirements: the Products, Shipping and VAT rules in `README.md`.
+- Tests to cover each acceptance point are added under `test/`.
